<p>(a)<img alt="the=" data-height="276" data-width="349" style="width: 257px; height: 203px;" width="257px" height="203px" class="internal" loading="lazy" src="https://chem.libretexts.org/@api/deki/files/459992/fa99ecd3fd3aab0cc709217dec317c2229f41ef6?revision=1&amp;size=bestfit&amp;width=257&amp;height=203" /> (b)&nbsp;<img alt="The ball-and-stick model has a benzene ring. C 1 is bonded to an aldehyde group. C 4 is bonded to a methyl group." data-height="273" data-width="385" style="width: 284px; height: 201px;" width="284px" height="201px" class="scaled-down-30 first-element internal" loading="lazy" src="https://chem.libretexts.org/@api/deki/files/459991/cc03da478171d9ec381c182f60e7f3de389a542a?revision=1&amp;size=bestfit&amp;width=284&amp;height=201" /></p>

